Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:03:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - legacy PlayerChatEvent and ChatEvent on the
 sender's region

The region-threading base disabled the deprecated synchronous chat
events (their Waitable went to the main-thread queue, which nothing
drains), so legacy chat/format plugins listening only to them never saw
a message. With listeners they fire again in Paper's order, on the
thread that owns the sender, decided by the calling thread (LegacyChat),
not by Paper's async flag (Player#chat always passes false): inline when
the caller owns the player; from the asynchronous chat thread through
the player's entity scheduler while it waits, bounded (5 s to start,
5 s more to finish); from a tick thread that does not own the player
(global region scheduler, another region) as a continuation on the
player's next tick, never waiting. Cancel, message, format and
recipients are honoured as on Paper. The message is sent only by the
step that follows a completed event, so a message whose event could not
run in time is dropped and is never sent late.

